Unity USD Toolkit patch to Alembic 1.8.5 (archive https://github.com/alembic/alembic/archive/refs/tags/1.8.5.zip,
tag 1.8.5, commit f4e3cc33e4270ade9d076a2cac7a2a4409c61675): bounds and null checks in the Ogawa reader.

Applied by Native~/build_openusd.py to the checked archive, extracted where build_usd.py extracts it;
its SHA-256 is pinned in Native~/dependency-sources/<platform>.tsv (an archive-patch row). Every change
is marked "Unity USD Toolkit" in the source. Found by fuzzing the payload's usdAbc plugin, which reads
Alembic through this code; files Alembic writes read exactly as before.

1. AbcCoreOgawa/ReadUtil.cpp, ReadDimensions: a sample whose group entries are not data comes back
   as null IDataPtrs (IGroup::getData), which were dereferenced; a data block shorter than its
   16-byte key underflowed the element count. Above all, the dimensions and the data are separate
   blocks, and the reader sizes its buffer from the dimensions and copies the whole data block into
   it: dimensions smaller than the data wrote past the buffer (to a null one when they said 0). A
   plain POD array now has to fill exactly its data block, and a string array can hold no more
   strings than the block has bytes.
2. ReadData takes how many PODs (strings) its destination holds and writes no more: the string loops
   wrote one std::string per 0 byte in the data, however many the destination had. ReadArraySample,
   AprImpl::getAs (which reads and checks the dimensions again for this) and SprImpl::getSample pass
   it; a POD with no size (which divided by zero, a trap on x86_64) is refused.
3. AbcGeom/IGeomParam.h, getIndexed/getExpanded: null samples are refused, and each index has to
   name a value before getExpanded reads it.
4. AbcGeom/IXform.cpp: an xform op type outside XformOperationType is refused (it left the op with
   no channels, which XformSample::getMatrix read through a null pointer), and so is a sample whose
   .vals hold fewer values than the ops have channels (read past the heap buffer), a .vals that is
   not float64 or an .ops that is not uint8 (read or written as the wrong size), and a missing
   .vals sample. Found by the Linux fuzz run on 2026-10-17.

